This project references AMD HIP SDK, ROCm, hipBLASLt, Composable Kernel,
rocWMMA, Boost.Multiprecision, Catch2, GMP, FLINT, and related exact linear
algebra research systems. Optional CK and rocWMMA accelerator sources are
referenced through pinned Git submodules under `third_party/rocm`; vcpkg
packages and external SDKs remain under their respective licenses.

The rank48 mathematical coefficient matrices and canonical linear programs in
third_party/rank48 are from
Jean-Guillaume Dumas and the PLinOpt contributors, revision
7c2006504a67caf3071ed4bd34ed772f6ed1a1a6, under CeCILL-B1.0. The unmodified
matrices, programs, license and exact provenance are retained there. The generated
rank48_program.hpp and rank48_slp.hpp tables derive from those artifacts.
RNS8's strict arithmetic importer, independent tensor checker, live-slot lowering
and execution kernels are original code. Upstream program text is parsed as
licensed arithmetic data; no PLinOpt executable or general code is executed.

